.TH SENDFILE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
sendfile \- transfer bytes between descriptors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/sendfile.h>
.B ssize_t sendfile(int output, int input, off_t* offset, size_t count);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Transfers up to count bytes from input to output. If offset is non\-NULL,
the pointed\-to offset is updated and the input file position is unchanged.
Otherwise the input file position is advanced. Transfers may be short;
Linux descriptor and offset restrictions apply.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns bytes transferred, zero at EOF, or \-1 with errno set.
Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sendfile (2)
